    "result_text": "All date-derived values now use the fiscal year, and the full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI moved every date-derived value onto a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starts 1 July, named by the calendar year it ends in \u2014 e.g. a registration on 2026-09-07 falls in FY27).\n\n**New shared helper** \u2014 `rest/function/owner/FiscalYears.java`:\n- `of(date)` \u2192 fiscal-year number (`month \u2265 7 ? year+1 : year`)\n- `label(date)` \u2192 `FY<YY>` string\n- `elapsed(start, end)` \u2192 whole fiscal years between two dates\n\n**Changes wired to it:**\n- **`fiscalYear` (new response field)** \u2014 added to `openapi.yml` (readOnly `FY<YY>` string) and mapped in `OwnerMapper.fiscalYear(owner)`, derived from the business-day-adjusted `registrationDate` (`null` for legacy owners without a date). This satisfies the acceptance test's `FY\\d{2}` regex.\n- **Membership identifier's year segment** \u2014 `OwnerMapper.membershipNumber` and `AuditOwnerCreated.membershipNumber` now use `FiscalYears.of(...)` instead of the calendar year, so `M<YY>` is the fiscal year (verified in the audit log: `membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M27`).\n- **Tenure** \u2014 `Memberships.hasTenureForPoints` now awards `TENURE_POINTS` when more than one *elapsed fiscal year* has passed (`FiscalYears.elapsed(registrationDate, now) > 1`), replacing the old 365-day window. A freshly created owner still has zero tenure.\n\nDescriptions/Javadoc in `openapi.yml`, `OwnerMapper`, `Memberships`, and `AuditOwnerCreated` were updated to reflect the fiscal-year semantics.\n\nOne convention decision worth flagging: the spec gives `FY<YY>` without pinning whether `YY` is the fiscal year's starting or ending calendar year. I used the standard Australian convention (named by the ending year, so July\u2013Dec roll to the next year). The lone acceptance test only checks the `FY\\d{2}` shape, so if you intended the *starting*-year convention instead, it's a one-line change in `FiscalYears.of`.",
